    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable matchups against mid-tier starting pitching. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting from a premium leadoff spot and a significant 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Phillips. Close behind is **Christian Yelich** (75.84), who leverages a 13% platoon efficiency gain to exploit the matchup against Singer. Both **Yordan Alvarez** (68.04) and **Caleb Durbin** (65.89) provide high-floor production, with the latter remaining a focal point for our strategy given his ability to weaponize his speed against Bradish, despite a slight deduction for the opposing battery\u2019s efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Colt Keith** (45.59), who was the first player excluded from the starting nine. While **Colt Keith** possesses solid underlying metrics, he was pushed to the bench due to the oppressive 2.89 xERA of opposing starter Williams, which heavily suppressed his efficiency score compared to the aggressive matchups presented to **Josh Smith** (60.34) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (59.80). Conversely, we are keeping **Carson Benge** (36.46) and **Dillon Dingler** (33.13) benched as their projected outputs fall well below the Zebras' 40.0 efficiency floor. We continue to monitor the status of **Gary Sanchez**, who remains benched as he is currently outside the official starting lineup. Managers should note that while **Trea Turner** (65.60) carries a strong projection, the matchup against Mahle\u2019s 3.97 xERA serves as a reminder that we must remain vigilant regarding in-game substitutions should any weather-related volatility emerge in the late afternoon windows.",
